@journal "I've met someone at school that I keep thinking about."
  @when story.taylor_school_interactions_counter >= 5

  @passage start

  @choice "Taylor" -> .taylor
    @effect set local.school_person "taylor"
  @endchoice

  @passage taylor

  There's this person at school, Taylor, who seems really...

  @choice "interesting" -> .interesting
    @effect set local.taylor_impression "interesting"
  @endchoice

  @choice "strange" -> .strange
    @effect set local.taylor_impression "strange"
  @endchoice

  @choice "annoying" -> .annoying
    @effect set local.taylor_impression "annoying"
  @endchoice

  @choice "attractive" -> .attractive
    @effect set local.taylor_impression "attractive"
    @effect set flags.journal.taylor_attractive
  @endchoice

  @passage interesting

  ...interesting. {{npc.taylor.subject | cap}} has this way of standing out without seeming like {{npc.taylor.subject}} is trying to.

  I'm hoping to...

  @choice "get to know Taylor better" -> .friend
    @effect set local.taylor_intent "friend"
  @endchoice

  @choice "get closer to Taylor" -> .closer
    @effect set local.taylor_intent "closer"
    @effect set flags.journal.wants_to_get_closer_to_taylor
  @endchoice

  @choice "keep my distance for now" -> .distance
    @effect set local.taylor_intent "distance"
  @endchoice

  @passage strange

  ...strange, honestly. I haven't decided whether {{npc.taylor.subject}} is the good kind of weird yet.

  Still, I'm hoping to...

  @choice "get to know Taylor better" -> .friend
    @effect set local.taylor_intent "friend"
  @endchoice

  @choice "flirt a little and see what happens" -> .closer
    @effect set local.taylor_intent "closer"
    @effect set flags.journal.wants_to_get_closer_to_taylor
  @endchoice

  @choice "avoid Taylor when I can" -> .distance
    @effect set local.taylor_intent "distance"
  @endchoice

  @passage annoying

  ...annoying. Maybe that's unfair this early, but Taylor has already managed to get under my skin.

  For now I think I'll...

  @choice "give Taylor another chance" -> .friend
    @effect set local.taylor_intent "friend"
  @endchoice

  @choice "see if the irritation is actually chemistry" -> .closer
    @effect set local.taylor_intent "closer"
    @effect set flags.journal.wants_to_get_closer_to_taylor
  @endchoice

  @choice "stay out of Taylor's way" -> .distance
    @effect set local.taylor_intent "distance"
  @endchoice

  @passage attractive

  ...really attractive. There, I wrote it down. Taylor is hot. That's probably going to make school more complicated than it needs to be.

  Maybe I should...

  @choice "get to know Taylor normally first" -> .friend
    @effect set local.taylor_intent "friend"
  @endchoice

  @choice "flirt and see where it goes" -> .closer
    @effect set local.taylor_intent "closer"
    @effect set flags.journal.wants_to_get_closer_to_taylor
  @endchoice

  @choice "not make a thing out of it" -> .distance
    @effect set local.taylor_intent "distance"
  @endchoice

  @passage friend

  ...actually get to know {{npc.taylor.object}} better. No point deciding what Taylor is like from one impression.

  @finish

  @passage closer

  ...get a little closer to {{npc.taylor.object}}, y'know, see where things go. Maybe there's something there. Maybe not. It could be fun finding out.

  @finish

  @passage distance

  ...keep some distance and see what happens. First impressions aren't everything, but I don't have to force myself to like everyone I meet.

  @finish
@endjournal

@journal "I actually got a job."
  @when flags.cafe_employee

  @passage start

  @random
    I got hired at the cafe. It's not exactly glamorous, but having somewhere I can turn an hour into money feels pretty important right now.
  @or
    So, apparently I work at the cafe now. It isn't glamorous, but having somewhere I can turn an hour into money feels pretty important right now.
  @endrandom

  The part I'm most worried about is...

  @choice "dealing with customers" -> .customers
    @effect set local.cafe_worry "customers"
  @endchoice

  @choice "messing something up" -> .mistakes
    @effect set local.cafe_worry "mistakes"
  @endchoice

  @choice "getting bored out of my mind" -> .boredom
    @effect set local.cafe_worry "boredom"
  @endchoice

  @choice "nothing, really" -> .fine
    @effect set local.cafe_worry "nothing"
  @endchoice

  @passage customers

  Customers, definitely. One rude person can turn an easy shift into an hour that feels five times longer. I'll just have to learn how to deal with them.

  @finish

  @passage mistakes

  Messing something up. Everyone screws up at a new job, obviously, but knowing that doesn't make the idea of doing it in front of a customer any nicer.

  @finish

  @passage boredom

  Getting bored. I can already imagine staring at the clock during a dead hour and wondering how sixty minutes can possibly take that long.

  @finish

  @passage fine

  Nothing in particular. It's a casual cafe job, not a life-or-death commitment. I can show up, work, get paid, and go home.

  @finish
@endjournal

@journal "The rent situation is completely ridiculous."
  @when flags.rent_intro_2 or flags.rent_landlord_visit_seen or flags.rent_intro_bypassed

  @passage start

  Apparently I owe rent from before I even properly settled in here. Somehow that has become my problem.

  Right now I mostly feel...

  @choice "angry" -> .angry
    @effect set local.rent_feeling "angry"
  @endchoice

  @choice "worried" -> .worried
    @effect set local.rent_feeling "worried"
  @endchoice

  @choice "confused" -> .confused
    @effect set local.rent_feeling "confused"
  @endchoice

  @choice "resigned" -> .resigned
    @effect set local.rent_feeling "resigned"
  @endchoice

  @passage angry

  Angry. I just moved in and I'm already being chased over money. I don't care how tidy the paperwork looks; it still feels absurd.

  @finish

  @passage worried

  Worried. Rent isn't optional, and neither is having somewhere to live. I need to make sure this doesn't get bad enough to threaten that.

  @finish

  @passage confused

  Confused. The dates, the notice, the whole situation feel like they belong to somebody else's life and somehow landed on my doorstep.

  @finish

  @passage resigned

  Resigned, mostly. Whether it makes sense or not, arguing with the amount won't magically make it disappear. I need money and a plan.

  @finish
@endjournal

@journal "I found something strange in my room."
  @when flags.quest.receptacles.start

  @passage start

  There is some kind of seamless receptacle sitting in my room now. I found it while unpacking, and I still have no idea what it is or why it was here.

  My first reaction is mostly...

  @choice "curiosity" -> .curious
    @effect set local.receptacle_reaction "curious"
  @endchoice

  @choice "unease" -> .uneasy
    @effect set local.receptacle_reaction "uneasy"
  @endchoice

  @choice "annoyance" -> .annoyed
    @effect set local.receptacle_reaction "annoyed"
  @endchoice

  @choice "nothing much" -> .shrug
    @effect set local.receptacle_reaction "indifferent"
  @endchoice

  @passage curious

  Curiosity. Something that strange does not just end up in a room by accident. I want to figure out what it does, even if I have no idea where to start.

  @finish

  @passage uneasy

  Unease. An object I cannot open, move, or explain is not exactly what I wanted to discover in my new home. I would feel better if I knew what it was for.

  @finish

  @passage annoyed

  Annoyance. I finally finished unpacking and immediately inherited a new problem that apparently cannot even be moved out of the way.

  @finish

  @passage shrug

  Not much, really. It is weird, but until it actually does something, it can sit there and be weird on its own time.

  @finish
@endjournal

@journal "I made it through every class today."
  @when flags.journal.completed_school_first_day or flags.journal.completed_school_day

  @passage start

  @if flags.journal.completed_school_first_day
    I made it through every class on my very first day of school. I actually followed the whole timetable from beginning to end.
  @else
    I finally made it through a complete day of school. It was not my first day, but this time I attended every class from beginning to end.
  @endif

  By the time the last class ended, I felt...

  @choice "proud of myself" -> .proud
    @effect set local.full_school_day_feeling "proud"
  @endchoice

  @choice "completely exhausted" -> .exhausted
    @effect set local.full_school_day_feeling "exhausted"
  @endchoice

  @choice "surprised it was not worse" -> .surprised
    @effect set local.full_school_day_feeling "surprised"
  @endchoice

  @passage proud

  ...proud of myself. Showing up for all of it might be ordinary for everyone else, but it still feels like something worth writing down.

  @finish

  @passage exhausted

  ...completely exhausted. A full timetable is a lot longer when I actually sit through every part of it.

  @finish

  @passage surprised

  ...surprised it was not worse. The day was long, but I made it through without wanting to run for the gates.

  @finish
@endjournal
